        "comments": "The assembly ddMalSylv1.hap1.2 is based on 42x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Haplotypic inversion detected on Chromosome 3 from 28 to 30.5 Mbp and on Chromosome 15 from 6.43 to 8.24 Mbp. The order and orientation may be uncertain on Chromosome 10 from 9.40 to 11.30 Mbp and on Chromosome 17 from 17 to 18.2 Mbp.",
